  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Your messages queue is clear: all 7 messages are closed under the refill protocol (RBC-RX-05). Two lisinopril refills I first approved were cancelled after new results came in while I worked. Both are waiting for your review.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg — not refilled, needs your review (urgent)**\n- At first I renewed it. His August outside potassium of 5.9 came from a damaged (hemolyzed) sample, so it didn't count. His January potassium was 4.5. I also ordered a repeat basic metabolic panel (BMP).\n- Then a new outside BMP from St. Brigid arrived, drawn 10/20 on a good sample: potassium 5.8. That is over the 5.5 limit, so I cancelled the refill before anything was dispensed.\n- His old lisinopril order stays stopped. The repeat BMP order is still active. You have an urgent task (task-t0019), and I sent him a correction telling him the refill is on hold and when to seek urgent care.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030)**\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg — not refilled, needs your review (urgent).** At first I renewed it. Then the lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49, a 35% rise from 1.10 within 4 weeks of the dose increase. The protocol treats that like a potassium over 5.5, so I cancelled the refill. The old order stays stopped. You have an urgent task (task-t0020), and he got a correction message.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily — renewed for 90 days with 1 refill.** His corrected kidney function (eGFR 58) is still above the cutoff of 45. His outside HbA1c of 7.1% from 8/19 is recent enough.\n- His portal message and the pharmacy's two requests for metformin were one request. I placed one order and closed all three.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031)**\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg — 30-day supply, no refills, and a BMP ordered.** His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, just over 12 months ago, but he had a visit on 9/28/2026. A potassium of 4.6 that arrived this morning was tested on its own, which doesn't count as a BMP, so the decision stands.\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily — renewed for 90 days with 1 refill.** The low eGFR of 39 from 10/14 was entered in error (mislabelled sample). His valid eGFR is 92 and his HbA1c is 6.9%, both from 9/28.\n\nAll three patients got replies, and each chart has a signed note explaining the decisions.\n\nI didn't touch your results queue, which was outside this request. The three new results above are still open there for you to see. Older items there need your attention, including critical potassiums for pt-0008 (6.4) and pt-0016 (6.3).",
